@prefix agp: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov#> .
@prefix bl: <https://dagalog.no/ns/backlog#> .
@prefix ghissues: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/issues/> .
@prefix ghpull: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/pull/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix session: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov/session#> .

# PROSPECTIVE summary scaffold, generated by scripts/new-provenance-summary.sh.
# TODO: replace the placeholder summaryText/decisionPoint below with the
# actual distilled reasoning behind this PR before committing — see
# docs/plans/TRANSCRIPT_SUMMARY_GUIDELINES.md. Timestamps below are real
# (from `git log main..HEAD` on branch issue-567-agentprov-session-deref); everything else that
# isn't marked TODO can be left as-is.

ghpull:601 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "sparql_endpoint, deploy: dereference agp:AgentSession hash-URIs (#567)" ;
    bl:number 601 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:567 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr601 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:567 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-08-13T22:23:27+02:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-08-26T20:17:15Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr601Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #567 (filed by #493, PR #562) asked for a working dereference story for GET /ns/agentprov/session: agp:AgentSession individuals are minted as hash-URIs under that namespace, but deploy/Caddyfile's /ns/agentprov handle is an exact match, so the fragment-stripped request 404s for every session:* IRI in the repo's own provenance data. The issue named two options -- a dynamically-generated namespace document, or migrating agp:AgentSession minting to slash-URIs under #493's /id/* scheme -- and asked to validate which is more tractable against real data flow rather than assume. Investigation (recorded in docs/plans/AGENTPROV_SESSION_DEREF_567_PLAN.md) found: production's Datastore never loads provenance/summaries/*.ttl (docker-compose.public.yml's dagalog service passes a single --data /data/dataset.ttl, same gap PR #562 already filed #565 for), and the production runtime container never has the provenance/ directory on disk at all (the Dockerfile's final stage copies only the compiled binary). This ruled out a design reading files from disk at request time, and confirmed 'query the live Datastore' (matching #562's own /describe precedent) was the only viable meaning of 'dynamically generated' today -- accepting the same open dependency on #565 that /describe already accepted, rather than filing a second, narrower 'wire production data' follow-up. A standalone regeneration-script alternative (a backlog-regenerate-style binary writing a static file for Caddy to serve, like #441's two vocabulary files) was considered and rejected: it would add a second manual regeneration lifecycle that goes stale between runs, on top of duplicating logic scripts/serve-backlog.sh's --data mechanism already provides generically. The chosen route (GET /ns/agentprov/session in sparql_endpoint/src/agentprov_session.rs) differs from /describe in three ways, each traced to a real difference in what's being served: outbound-only (a namespace document describes the resources it defines, not a resource's full neighbourhood, unlike a single bl:Issue's inbound-heavy description); 200 rather than 404 when the store holds no session data (a namespace document for an empty set is still a valid document); and unauthenticated at the Caddy edge, unlike /describe/id/* (this route only ever exposes session:* triples, and that data -- provenance/summaries/*.ttl -- is already public in the repo, unlike /describe's arbitrary live dataset content, which the SPARQL endpoint itself requires auth to read). Hit the documented shared-CARGO_TARGET_DIR stale-incremental-artifact hazard twice while validating locally (a freshly-touched, freshly-compiled test binary intermittently served pre-route-registration 404s from what looked like the same binary hash); resolved both times by touching the affected files and rebuilding, per CLAUDE.md's own documented fix, and cross-checked against a directly-run dagalog binary with curl to confirm the route genuinely worked before trusting the test run." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:601 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr601 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr601Decision .

session:pr601Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Implemented GET /ns/agentprov/session as a live route in sparql_endpoint querying the Datastore for session:* subject triples, mirroring #493's /describe route, and accepted the same 'production Datastore doesn't have this data yet' gap #565 already tracks." ;
    agp:alternative "Considered a standalone regeneration script (backlog-regenerate-style) that scans provenance/summaries/*.ttl and writes a static Turtle file for Caddy to serve, matching #441's static-file pattern for the two fixed vocabulary documents. Rejected: it introduces a second manual regeneration lifecycle (on top of backlog-regenerate's already-manual one) that silently goes stale whenever a new provenance/summaries/pr-<N>.ttl lands without someone re-running it, and duplicates the file-merging logic scripts/serve-backlog.sh's --data mechanism already provides generically." .
